i3lock-color (2.13.c.5-1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release (2.13.c.5)
  * Follow upstream to https://github.com/Raymo111/i3lock-color: the
    eBrnd repository this package used to build from has not been touched
    since 2016, and PandorasFox handed maintenance to Raymo111
  * debian/control:
    - Declare Conflicts, Replaces and Provides on i3lock. Upstream installs
      /usr/bin/i3lock, /usr/share/man/man1/i3lock.1, /etc/pam.d/i3lock and
      the i3lock shell completions, so the package could never unpack
      alongside i3lock; it is a drop-in replacement for it
    - Switch to debhelper-compat (= 13) and drop debian/compat
    - Bump Standards-Version to 4.7.4
    - Set Rules-Requires-Root: no
    - Mark the binary package Multi-Arch: foreign
    - Move from Section: utils to Section: x11
    - Add the build dependencies 2.13.c.5 needs that were missing:
      autoconf-archive, bash-completion, libfontconfig-dev and
      libxcb-xrm-dev
    - Drop the build dependencies configure.ac does not check for:
      libx11-dev (also listed twice), libx11-xcb-dev and libxkbfile-dev
    - Replace pkg-config with pkgconf and the obsolete libxcb-util0-dev
      with libxcb-util-dev
    - Point Homepage, Vcs-Browser and Vcs-Git at the current upstream and
      at this packaging repository
    - Rewrite the description, which still described plain i3lock
  * debian/rules:
    - Enable all hardening build flags
    - Configure with --disable-builddir; AX_ENABLE_BUILDDIR otherwise
      re-execs configure into a host-named subdirectory that debhelper
      cannot see
    - Pass --with-zsh-completion-dir explicitly so the zsh completion is
      shipped deterministically instead of depending on whether a zsh
      binary happens to exist in the build chroot
    - Rename the shell completions after dh_auto_install; upstream's
      install-data-hook does the rename without honouring DESTDIR, so a
      staged install left them as i3lock-bash and i3lock-zsh
    - Drop the commented-out dh_make boilerplate
  * debian/watch: add a watch file tracking upstream GitHub tags
  * debian/gbp.conf: add git-buildpackage configuration
  * debian/upstream/metadata: add upstream metadata
  * debian/copyright: point at the current upstream and record that the
    bundled tinyexpr is under the zlib licence

 -- Clay Risser <clay@clayrisser.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 21:30:00 +0100

